course: dictionary
lesson: 5671
title: Livery: uniform, colours, or stable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so context tells you which meaning is right. In «Alice thinks one is a footman because he was in livery», livery means the special uniform a servant wears, so the footman is dressed as a servant of a great house.
explain: The same word can also mean the colours and design of a company's vehicles. In «the airline's livery», livery means the paint scheme. Ask yourself: is this about clothes, colours, or a place? The other words in the sentence will tell you.
explain: Livery can also mean a livery stable, a place where horses are kept and fed for their owners, or hired out for payment. When you see a stable or yard nearby, the meaning is the horse place. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Livery means a special uniform, the colours of a company's vehicles, or a place where horses are kept and fed.
fact: «In livery» means wearing the special uniform of a servant, like the footmen in Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.
fact: A footman is a servant who opens doors and carries messages.
fact: A livery stable is a place where horses are kept and fed for their owners, or hired out for payment.
fact: Context clues help you choose the right meaning when a word has more than one.
exercise: In Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, what does «in livery» tell us about the footman? | He is a fish | He is asleep in the hall | He is painted in bright colours | *He is wearing the special uniform of a servant
exercise: «The airline's livery is blue and white.» What does livery mean here? | A place where horses are kept | *The colours and design of the company's planes | A uniform worn by servants | A small bird
exercise: «She took her horse to the livery stable every evening.» What is a livery stable? | A shop that sells paint | A school for riding | A house where servants live | *A place where horses are kept and fed for payment
test: In history, what was livery worn by servants of a great house? | *A special uniform | A type of horse | A bright paint on the walls | A kind of train ticket
test: «The bus had a red and gold livery.» What does livery mean? | A stable for horses | A ticket for travel | *The colours and design of the bus company | A servant's uniform
exam: Which meaning of livery fits «the footmen were in livery»? | A kind of paint for walls | The colours of a plane | A place where horses are kept | *A special uniform worn by servants
